    <string name="how_to_play_title">How to Play</string>
    <string name="how_to_play_intro">Tap a mode below for the full rules. The four duels (Reaction Duel, Reaction Rumble, Tap Battle, Endurance) can all be played as a Quick round or a Best of 3/5/7 championship -- points carry over between rounds and whoever has the most when the match ends is crowned Champion.</string>

    <string name="htp_reaction_title">Reaction Duel</string>
    <string name="htp_reaction_body">Two players each hold a finger on their half of the screen. After a random delay, the screen flashes \"GO!\" and the first to lift wins the point. Lifting before \"GO!\" is a false start and loses the round.</string>
    <string name="htp_rumble_title">Reaction Rumble</string>
    <string name="htp_rumble_body">Two to eight players all hold a finger down at once. After a random delay, the screen flashes \"GO!\" and the first to lift wins. Lifting early only disqualifies you for that round -- everyone else keeps playing.</string>
    <string name="htp_tapbattle_title">Tap Battle</string>
    <string name="htp_tapbattle_body">Two players place a finger on their half to ready up. After a 3-2-1 countdown, tap your side as fast as you can. First to reach the target number of taps wins the round.</string>
    <string name="htp_endurance_title">Endurance</string>
    <string name="htp_endurance_body">Two to eight players hold a finger down at once. As soon as everyone is down, the clock starts -- whoever lifts first is out. The last finger still touching the screen wins.</string>
    <string name="htp_single_title">Finger Picker: Single Pick</string>
    <string name="htp_single_body">Everyone places a finger anywhere on the screen -- no need to say how many people are playing first. Once fingers stop arriving, the app spins through everyone and lands on one at random. Choose a purpose before you start: Who Pays, Who\'s It, Goes First, Truth or Dare, or write your own.</string>
    <string name="htp_order_title">Finger Picker: Full Order</string>
    <string name="htp_order_body">Works just like Single Pick, but instead of stopping after one winner it keeps picking fingers one at a time until everyone has a rank -- handy for turn order, team drafts, or deciding a whole night\'s chore rotation in one go.</string>
    <string name="htp_teamsplit_title">Finger Picker: Team Split</string>
    <string name="htp_teamsplit_body">Everyone places a finger, then the app randomly and evenly divides the group into Team A and Team B -- a quick way to pick teams for anything.</string>
</resources>
